<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Mellifont</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1603</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war-ireland">Nine Years' War (Ireland)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Mellifont was the submission of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-oneill-earl-of-tyrone">Hugh O'Neill, Earl of Tyrone</a>, to Lord Mountjoy at Mellifont in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-louth">County Louth</a> in March 1603, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war-ireland">Nine Years' War</a>. O'Neill renounced his Gaelic title and accepted English law but kept most of his lands; he had not been told that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-i">Elizabeth I</a> had died days earlier. Growing pressure on his position led to the Flight of the Earls in 1607.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-mellifont.jpg" alt="Treaty of Mellifont" width="320" height="201" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TyroneSubmitstoMountjoy.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
